Active Directory depends heavily on DNS.

You already know DNS from Linux:

google.com → IP address

For example:

google.com
     ↓
142.x.x.x

In an Active Directory environment, DNS does more than simply resolve names.

It helps computers find the Domain Controller and Active Directory services.

For eg:

PC01
  |
  | "Where is my Domain Controller?"
  ↓
DNS
  |
  ↓
SERVER01

Your lab will look like:

             SERVER01
        Windows Server 2025
                 |
       +---------+---------+
       |                   |
      AD DS               DNS
       |
       ↓
Domain Controller
